WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.983
The year is 1956.

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:06.038
You work in a pharmacology laboratory at Western
Reserve University in Cleveland.

00:00:06.668 --> 00:00:10.153
You have made a homogenate of liver (liver
ground up in buffer).

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.135
Nothing in it is alive.

00:00:12.908 --> 00:00:17.904
At this time, most biologists think that a
hormone can act only on an intact, living cell.

00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:21.140
You spin the homogenate in a centrifuge.

00:00:21.744 --> 00:00:24.205
The membranes form a pellet at the bottom of the
tube.

00:00:24.776 --> 00:00:26.625
Above the pellet is a clear liquid.

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:32.821
The clear liquid contains phosphorylase, the
enzyme that starts the breakdown of stored
glycogen.

00:00:33.471 --> 00:00:36.296
Your only measurement is whether phosphorylase
is switched on.

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:37.746
You do three tests.

00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:40.308
1. You add adrenaline to the clear liquid.

00:00:40.699 --> 00:00:42.288
Phosphorylase stays off.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.914
2. You add adrenaline to the membranes.

00:00:45.465 --> 00:00:47.316
Again, phosphorylase stays off.

00:00:48.108 --> 00:00:51.119
3. You incubate adrenaline with the membranes.

00:00:51.728 --> 00:00:55.421
Then you remove the membranes and add the liquid
they were in to fresh clear liquid.

00:00:56.287 --> 00:00:58.108
Now phosphorylase switches on.

00:00:58.616 --> 00:01:00.585
Answer three questions in your own words.

00:01:01.398 --> 00:01:04.743
1. Tests 1 and 3 both end with adrenaline in
clear liquid.

00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:07.775
Only test 3 switches phosphorylase on.

00:01:08.295 --> 00:01:08.650
Why?

00:01:09.423 --> 00:01:12.929
2. How far into the cell does adrenaline itself
reach?

00:01:13.494 --> 00:01:15.243
What carries the signal after that point?

00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:19.199
3. What one experiment would show that you are
right?

00:01:19.551 --> 00:01:22.347
Earl Sutherland and Theodore Rall ran these
tests in Cleveland.

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:24.178
Here is what the tests showed.

00:01:24.646 --> 00:01:26.491
Adrenaline never enters the liver cell.

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:30.645
It binds to a receptor, a protein in the cell's
outer membrane.

00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:34.780
The bound receptor switches on a second protein
in the same membrane.

00:01:35.464 --> 00:01:39.095
This second protein is an enzyme, adenylyl
cyclase.

00:01:39.678 --> 00:01:42.797
It converts the cell's own ATP into a new
molecule.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:49.937
In the new molecule, the phosphate is attached
to the sugar at two points, so the molecule is
closed into a small ring.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.542
Its name is cyclic AMP.

00:01:53.286 --> 00:02:00.147
Cyclic AMP is small, and it moves freely through
the inside of the cell, where the hormone cannot
go.

00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:07.134
One bound hormone keeps its enzyme active long
enough to make hundreds of cyclic AMP molecules.

00:02:07.816 --> 00:02:11.909
So a short contact outside the cell produces a
large signal inside.

00:02:12.708 --> 00:02:18.542
Sutherland called the hormone the first
messenger and cyclic AMP the second messenger.

00:02:19.425 --> 00:02:22.891
In your tubes, the pellet held the membrane and
its enzyme.

00:02:23.578 --> 00:02:25.823
The clear liquid held phosphorylase.

00:02:26.343 --> 00:02:29.706
In the liver, cyclic AMP causes glycogen
breakdown.

00:02:30.256 --> 00:02:32.745
The same molecule has other effects in other
cells.

00:02:33.355 --> 00:02:35.757
In a fat cell it starts fat breakdown.

00:02:36.316 --> 00:02:38.486
In a heart cell it makes the heartbeat stronger.

00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:42.093
The effect depends on the proteins inside each
cell.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:47.517
Inside the cell, cyclic AMP switches on protein
kinase A.

00:02:48.224 --> 00:02:54.011
The kinase adds phosphate groups to a series of
target proteins, and this passes the signal on.

00:02:54.589 --> 00:02:59.304
Then an enzyme called phosphodiesterase destroys
cyclic AMP.

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:02.925
This ends the response until the next hormone
signal arrives.
